    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Can you explain the difference between high glycemic index foods and low glycemic index foods? I'm trying to understand how they affect blood sugar and insulin response for someone managing type 2 diabetes.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "High glycemic index (GI) foods cause a rapid spike in blood sugar because they are quickly digested, leading to a large insulin release. Conversely, low GI foods are broken down slowly, providing a steady release of glucose into the bloodstream. For managing type 2 diabetes, choosing low GI options helps prevent sharp blood sugar spikes. This gradual release supports more stable energy levels and better insulin sensitivity.",
