      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For breakfast, opt for steel-cut oats, eggs, or whole-grain toast with avocado instead of sugary cereals or white bread. At lunch, focus on lentils, quinoa, or brown rice paired with plenty of non-starchy vegetables like a large salad or roasted broccoli. Generally, incorporating fiber-rich whole foods rather than refined carbs is the key to keeping your meal's overall GI low.",
